---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import CTAFooter from "../components/CTAFooter.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — Vera AI"
  description="How Vera AI collects, uses, stores, and protects your data. What we log, what we redact, how long we keep it, and who can access it."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="privacy">
    <div class="privacy-inner">
      <header class="privacy-header">
        <div class="privacy-badge">Privacy</div>
        <h1>What Vera knows about you</h1>
        <p class="privacy-subtitle">
          Plain-English description of what data Vera collects, why we collect
          it, how long we keep it, who can see it, and how to ask us to
          delete it.
        </p>
        <p class="last-updated">Last updated: April 7, 2026</p>
      </header>

      <section class="callout">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul class="callout-list">
          <li>
            Vera is an LLM-based coding agent. To answer your prompts we send
            your conversation content to <strong>Anthropic</strong> (the model
            provider) and store observability data with <strong>Langfuse</strong>
            and on our own infrastructure.
          </li>
          <li>
            We <strong>redact</strong> known secrets and common personal
            identifiers (API keys, JWTs, database connection strings, email
            addresses, credit-card numbers, SSNs) before any conversation
            content is written to disk or sent to an observability vendor.
          </li>
          <li>
            We retain conversation snapshots and execution logs for
            <strong>7 days</strong>, then delete them from both local disk and
            our object storage.
          </li>
          <li>
            We do <strong>not</strong> sell your data, use it to train models,
            or share it with advertisers.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can request full deletion at any time by emailing
            <a href="mailto:privacy@agent-army.ai">privacy@agent-army.ai</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Three categories of data: conversation content, integration
          metadata, and operational telemetry.
        </p>

        <div class="card-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Conversation data</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Prompts you send Vera through Slack, Linear, GitHub, or the CLI</li>
              <li>Vera's replies, including intermediate reasoning</li>
              <li>Tool calls Vera makes (read file, run bash, search web, query Linear, etc.) and their results</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Integration metadata</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Slack:</strong> workspace, channel, thread timestamp, author user ID</li>
              <li><strong>Linear:</strong> organization, issue identifier, issue title, comment author</li>
              <li><strong>GitHub:</strong> repository, PR/issue number, comment author, comment type</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Operational telemetry</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Token usage and computed cost per turn</li>
              <li>Tool execution latencies</li>
              <li>Session lifecycle events (start, end, retry, compaction)</li>
              <li>Scrubbed error messages and stack traces</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>What we don't collect</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Payment card data — handled directly by our payment processor</li>
              <li>Cookies, device IDs, browser fingerprints</li>
              <li>Biometric or location data</li>
              <li>Anything used to train or fine-tune models</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>2. Why we collect it</h2>
        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Data used</th>
                <th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Run the agent and respond to your prompts</td>
                <td>Conversation data, integration metadata</td>
                <td>Performance of a contract</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Crash recovery — resume sessions after a restart</td>
                <td>Conversation snapshots</td>
                <td>Legitimate interest (service continuity)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Debugging and incident response</td>
                <td>Execution logs, error traces</td>
                <td>Legitimate interest (operating the service)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Cost accounting and capacity planning</td>
                <td>Token usage, latencies</td>
                <td>Legitimate interest (running the business)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Security monitoring and abuse prevention</td>
                <td>Logs, error traces</td>
                <td>Legitimate interest (security)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="emphasis">
          We do <strong>not</strong> use your conversation data to train or
          fine-tune any model.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>3. Who else sees your data</h2>
        <p>
          To deliver Vera we share data with a small set of third-party
          subprocessors — model providers, observability vendors, and platform
          integrations. Each one is listed with its purpose, the data it
          receives, and where it's processed on our
          <a href="/subprocessors" class="inline-link">subprocessors page</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          We will notify customers at least <strong>30 days</strong> before
          adding a new subprocessor.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>4. How long we keep it</h2>
        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Data category</th>
                <th>Where it lives</th>
                <th>Retention</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Conversation snapshots (recovery)</td>
                <td>Tenant Fly volume + Tigris S3</td>
                <td>7 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Session execution logs</td>
                <td>Tenant Fly volume + Tigris S3</td>
                <td>7 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Active session registry</td>
                <td>Tenant Fly volume + Tigris S3</td>
                <td>Pruned after 24 hours of inactivity</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Langfuse traces</td>
                <td>Langfuse Cloud</td>
                <td>Up to 30 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>OAuth tokens (Slack, Linear, GitHub)</td>
                <td>Encrypted database</td>
                <td>Lifetime of your account; deleted on uninstall</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          After the retention windows above pass, the data is irrecoverable
          from our systems. Data held by sub-processors (Slack messages,
          Linear comments, GitHub PR comments) is governed by those
          platforms' own policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>5. How we protect your data</h2>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Redaction before storage</h3>
        <p>
          Before any conversation content is written to disk or sent to an
          observability vendor, it passes through a scrubber that redacts
          known secret formats, authentication tokens, connection strings,
          and common personal identifiers such as email addresses and
          payment card numbers.
        </p>
        <p>
          For tools that produce large or sensitive bodies (file reads, bash
          output, Linear issue bodies, web search results), the scrubber
          stores only a byte-count summary in traces — never the raw body.
        </p>
        <p class="caveat">
          The scrubber is best-effort and pattern-based. It will not catch
          every form of sensitive data — free-form names, addresses, and
          identifiers that don't match a known pattern can pass through.
          Treat Vera the way you'd treat a chat with a co-worker: don't paste
          anything you wouldn't want a colleague to see in a debug log.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Encryption</h3>
        <p>
          All network traffic between Vera and sub-processors uses TLS. Tigris
          encrypts bucket contents at rest. Fly.io volumes are encrypted at
          rest. OAuth tokens are encrypted with AES-256-GCM before being
          written to the database — see the
          <a href="/security" class="inline-link">security page</a> for the
          full key-storage architecture.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sub-heading">Tenant isolation</h3>
        <p>
          Each workspace runs on its own dedicated machine. There is no
          shared runtime, shared filesystem, or shared in-memory state
          between tenants.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>6. Who can access your conversations</h2>
        <p>
          Operators of Vera (the Vera AI engineering team) can view full
          conversation traces in our observability tooling and can access
          tenant data via cloud provider credentials. This access is governed
          by our internal access policy and used only for incident response,
          debugging at customer request, and security investigations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Anthropic, Langfuse, Tigris, and Fly.io employees can access data
          in their respective systems under their published access policies.
          See each vendor's trust documentation for details.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are working toward a tighter posture — per-tenant observability
          isolation, formal break-glass procedures with customer notification,
          and an in-product audit log of who viewed which conversation. If
          your organization requires any of these as a precondition for
          adoption, please reach out at
          <a href="mailto:privacy@agent-army.ai">privacy@agent-army.ai</a>
          and we'll work with you on a path.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you are located, you may have the following
          rights regarding your personal data:
        </p>
        <ul class="rights-list">
          <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the data we hold about you</li>
          <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — correct inaccurate data</li>
          <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — request that we delete your data</li>
          <li><strong>Restriction</strong> — request that we limit how we process your data</li>
          <li><strong>Portability</strong> — request your data in a machine-readable format</li>
          <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, email
          <a href="mailto:privacy@agent-army.ai">privacy@agent-army.ai</a>.
          We complete deletion requests within <strong>30 days</strong>.
        </p>
        <p class="caveat">
          We can only delete data we still hold. Conversation snapshots and
          logs older than 7 days have already been removed automatically.
          Data held by Slack, Linear, or GitHub is governed by those
          platforms' own policies — we can delete what Vera stores about an
          interaction, but not the original Slack message or Linear comment.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>8. International data transfers</h2>
        <p>
          Vera is operated from the United States. If you are located outside
          the United States, your data may be transferred to, and processed
          in, the United States. Where required, we rely on Standard
          Contractual Clauses with our sub-processors for transfers from the
          EEA, UK, and Switzerland.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>9. Children's data</h2>
        <p>
          Vera is not directed to children under 16. We do not knowingly
          collect personal data from children under 16. If you believe a
          child has used Vera, please email
          <a href="mailto:privacy@agent-army.ai">privacy@agent-army.ai</a>
          and we will delete the relevant data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>10. Changes to this notice</h2>
        <p>
          We will update this notice when our practices change. Material
          changes will be communicated through Vera's integration channels
          and through the project's changelog. The <strong>Last updated</strong>
          date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="contact">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions, deletion requests, or anything else covered
          on this page, email
          <a href="mailto:privacy@agent-army.ai">privacy@agent-army.ai</a>.
          For security vulnerability reports, email
          <a href="mailto:security@agent-army.ai">security@agent-army.ai</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <CTAFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding: 8rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .privacy-inner {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .privacy-header {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .privacy-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.35rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.3);
    border-radius: 100px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .privacy-subtitle {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.2rem);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .last-updated {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    opacity: 0.7;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .callout {
    padding: 2.5rem;
    border: 2px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.2);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .callout h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .callout-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .callout-list li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .callout-list li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-text);
  }

  .callout-list strong,
  .callout-list a {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .callout-list a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .section > p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .section > p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .section .section-intro {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .section .sub-heading {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .section a {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .inline-link {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .card {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.12);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
  }

  .card h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .card ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .card li {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .card li::before {
    content: "—";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .card strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .table-wrapper {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
  }

  thead {
    border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.15);
  }

  th {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  td {
    padding: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.08);
  }

  tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .emphasis {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .emphasis strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .redaction-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .redaction-list li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    position: relative;
  }

  .redaction-list li::before {
    content: "✕";
    position: absolute;
    left: -1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    opacity: 0.5;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .redaction-list code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
    background: rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.06);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .rights-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .rights-list li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    position: relative;
  }

  .rights-list li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute;
    left: -1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .rights-list strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .caveat {
    font-size: 0.9rem !important;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-left: 3px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.2);
    background: rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.03);
    margin-top: 1rem !important;
  }

  .contact {
    padding: 2.5rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(13, 40, 24, 0.12);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
  }

  .contact h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .contact p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .contact a {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .privacy {
      padding: 4rem 1.5rem 2rem;
    }

    .card-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    th,
    td {
      padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
    }
  }
</style>
